        "text": "A support engineer types `ERR_2087` into your shiny RAG search box. Pure semantic search hands back three chunks about \"connection reset loops\" and \"session timeout recovery\" that are thematically adjacent and completely useless, while the one runbook that literally contains the string `ERR_2087` sits at position 34, far outside the top-k that ever reaches the model. Nobody threw that chunk away on purpose. The embedding did it quietly, at index time, and hybrid search exists because that failure is structural, not a bug you can prompt your way out of."
