        "kind": "p",
        "text": "Once a benchmark is the thing everyone optimizes, Goodhart's Law kicks in and the measure stops measuring. *The Leaderboard Illusion* documented this on Chatbot Arena, which ranks models with a **Bradley-Terry** model over human pairwise votes. It found an undisclosed private-testing policy: providers could submit many private variants and publish only the best. Meta tested **27** private variants ahead of the Llama-4 launch (verified). Selecting the max of N noisy scores is upward-biased by construction, so the published rank is inflated before a single real user sees the model."
