        "kind": "p",
        "text": "The more damaging finding was overfitting to the arena's own distribution. Fine-tuning on progressively more arena data lifted win-rate on the in-distribution ArenaHard test from **23.5%** to **49.9%**, a **+112%** relative gain, while the same models did not improve on MMLU (figures verified). That is the signature of learning the test, not the task. Meanwhile data access was lopsided (OpenAI, Google, Meta, and Anthropic together received an estimated **62.8%** of all arena data) and about **205** models were silently deprecated versus **47** officially listed, quietly reshaping the rankings (verified)."
