        "kind": "p",
        "text": "The math is unforgiving once you chain steps. A call that is right 99% of the time sounds shippable. Put five of them in an agent loop and end-to-end reliability is **0.99^5 = 0.951**, so about **4.9%** of full runs fail somewhere (calculated). A 99% average and a 95% end-to-end reliability are different numbers, and your users feel the second one. That is why the number you ship on should be worst-case pass-rate on your own cases, not benchmark mean accuracy."
