        "caption": "Product eval measures pass@all, correct on every run of the same input. Average accuracy rewards 'usually fine'; this rewards 'never wrong on the cases I chose to care about.'",
        "code": "# Product eval: worst-case reliability, not average accuracy.\nK = 5  # runs per example\n\ndef evaluate(model, golden):\n    reliable = 0\n    for ex in golden:                    # golden = your real, labeled cases\n        outs = [model(ex.prompt) for _ in range(K)]\n        # capability: did it EVER get it right?\n        # reliability: did it get it right EVERY time?\n        if all(judge(o, ex.expected) for o in outs):\n            reliable += 1\n    return reliable / len(golden)         # pass@all: the number you ship on"
