        "text": "Your agent keeps referencing a file that doesn't exist. So you add a paragraph to the system prompt swearing the path is real. Next run it invents a different path. You were tuning the wrong thing the whole time: a language model is a function from text to text, and no amount of text tells it what is actually on disk. The fix isn't a bigger prompt. It's giving the model a computer it can look at, poke, and get answers back from."
