        "kind": "p",
        "text": "So the discipline is: keep one loop with excellent tools; when context gets long, compress the trace instead of forking; graduate to a manager-plus-subagents design only when the work is genuinely breadth-first, high-value enough to eat 15x tokens, and you've accepted that gathering can be parallel but the merge should not be. Multi-agent is a real tool. It just isn't the default, and treating it as one is how you pay premium tokens to ship Mario when you asked for Flappy Bird."
