        "caption": "Illustrative, with the math shown in the next paragraph. Blended cost scales linearly with the share of traffic you send to the frontier model. The point of a router is to keep that share small without dropping quality.",
        "diagram": "xychart-beta\n    title \"Blended cost vs frontier share\"\n    x-axis [\"0\", \"20\", \"50\", \"80\", \"100\"]\n    y-axis \"Cost $/Mtok\" 0 --> 5\n    line [0.5, 1.4, 2.75, 4.1, 5]"
