        "kind": "p",
        "text": "The other half of risk is data. `providerOptions.gateway.zeroDataRetention: true` forces the request onto a compliant provider, and if none can serve it the request fails with `no_providers_available` rather than silently leaking to a non-compliant one. The `only` filter restricts which providers are even eligible. This is routing by policy, not by cleverness, and it is where 'route to the best model' quietly becomes 'route to the model legal signed off on.'"
