        "kind": "p",
        "text": "Latency-sensitive paths care less about which provider and more about which one answers first. `providerTimeouts` sets a per-provider deadline (BYOK only) measured until the first token arrives. If a provider does not start streaming in time, the gateway aborts and fails over to the next one. The limits are a 1,000ms floor and a 789,000ms ceiling (about 13 minutes), and once the first token lands the timeout is cleared. Here is that failover playing out between two providers."
