        "text": "Notice what the fast boot buys you: you can afford to throw the box away after every task. That is the actual security property agents need. A long-lived sandbox accumulates state, and state an attacker touched is state you now have to trust. An ephemeral sandbox has a lifecycle measured in one task: create, run, capture what you need, destroy. Nothing the code did to the environment survives, so prompt-injection that plants a backdoor in `/usr/local/bin` gets vaporized on teardown."
