        "text": "Isolation stops the code from touching the host. It does nothing about the code eating the host. An agent that writes a runaway `while True: os.fork()` or spins up a miner will happily starve every other tenant on the machine. That is what cgroups are for, and for agent workloads they are not optional. Cap memory, cap CPU, and specifically cap the process count, because a `--pids-limit` is the difference between a fork bomb that gets killed and one that takes down the node."
