        "kind": "p",
        "text": "Ephemeral has a catch: if everything dies on teardown, so do the results. The generated report, the modified repo, the plot the code rendered, all of it is inside a filesystem you are about to wipe. So artifacts need an explicit, narrow channel out. The rule of thumb is that **artifacts are the only thing allowed to outlive the sandbox**, and they leave through one controlled path, not by giving the box write access to your real disk. In the Docker example that channel is a single mounted `/out` directory; on microVM platforms it is usually an API call that reads named files back before the VM is destroyed."
