        "text": "A staged rollout is only useful if something is watching. The two headline signals are **crash-free users** (or sessions) and, on Android, the **ANR rate**, surfaced by Play's Android Vitals, App Store Connect, or a crash reporter like Crashlytics or Sentry. The pattern that removes fear: pick a floor, and if crash-free drops below it during the staged window, auto-halt through the store API and page on-call. If the build soaks clean for your chosen window, auto-bump to the next step. The exact numbers are yours to tune; the ones below are illustrative."
