    "excerpt": "Meta generated the vast majority of Llama 3.1's fine-tuning data synthetically. Naive self-training does the opposite and rots the model. The difference is the quality loop: generation, verification, ranking, dedup, and decontamination. Here is how each piece works and exactly where it breaks.",
    "readingMinutes": 9,
    "slug": "synthetic-data",
    "title": "Synthetic Data Needs a Quality Loop"
